    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "BOS 29, HOU 29",
        "text": "An even opening quarter. Tari Eason hit two early threes off the Houston bench, and Luka Garza answered with threes of his own as the backup center."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "HOU 57, BOS 50",
        "text": "Houston won the quarter 28–21. Sengun had 12 first-half points on 6-of-8 shooting, and Mitchell Robinson briefly left with a sprained left thumb before returning. Boston closed the half on an 8–4 run capped by a Jayson Tatum three; Tatum had 11 points on 3-of-9 at the break."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "HOU 82, BOS 73",
        "text": "Robinson replaced Hugo González in the starting lineup for the second half, and Neemias Queta scored Boston's first 7 points of the quarter. Tatum then picked up two quick offensive fouls, both on charges drawn by Marcus Smart, and sat late in the quarter with four fouls as Boston went 6:17 without a field goal."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: HOU 109, BOS 93",
        "text": "Houston pulled away, with Smart hitting two late threes and Reed Sheppard scoring 8 in the quarter. Boston trailed by as many as 18, its largest deficit of the season, and was down 15 when Tatum checked out with 2:29 left. The Rockets outscored Boston 50–34 in the paint and 18–2 on fast breaks."
      }
